# Medicare

Federal health insurance program for people age 65 and older.

## Parts
- **Part A**: Hospital insurance (generally premium-free if eligible)
- **Part B**: Medical insurance (monthly premium + deductible)
- **Part D**: Prescription drug coverage (monthly premium)

## What Medicare Doesn't Cover
- Long-term care (nursing home)
- Most dental, vision, and hearing care
- Prescription drugs fully (Part D has gaps)
- Deductibles and co-pays

## Planning Considerations
Medicare is not comprehensive — significant out-of-pocket costs remain. Fidelity estimates a couple retiring at 65 faces $315,000 in lifetime healthcare costs, with $140,000 in Medicare premiums and $175,000 out-of-pocket.

